WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.430
Here's an interesting a certain sort of political
story is that it's a break.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:05.470
This is a political show.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.759
It's a break from the virus coverage.

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:12.550
And it's about Democratic New York Congresswoman
Alexandrea Castillo Cortez.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.670
She's getting crushed by a portion of the
left, a portion of the left.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:21.020
That widely supported her for a long time,
at least until recently.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:27.690
And the reason AOC is getting crushed is she
is taking what she sees as a more pragmatic

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.550
approach to the progressive movement.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:35.429
And it's a really, really interesting story
that has divided the online progressive left

00:00:35.429 --> 00:00:37.469
over the last few days.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:42.960
This all started because there are a whole
bunch of primary challenges by progressive

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.399
Democratic candidates against more centrist
Democratic incumbents.

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:52.470
AOC hasn't endorsed many of those progressive
challengers.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:58.010
She's chosen a couple of sort of easy ones
in Texas and Illinois, where the opponents

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.429
are really conservative Democrats who oppose
abortion.

00:01:01.429 --> 00:01:04.680
But otherwise, AOC has stayed out of a lot
of these races.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.060
AOC has also had quite a bit of turnover in
her staff.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:14.110
A lot of those sort of outspoken young progressive
activists that were working for AOC have been

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:21.530
replaced with some more moderate professional
political strategists, Democrats that often

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.850
work with incumbent Democrats.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:32.000
Now, there are questions increasingly about
whether AOC campaigned enough for Bernie before

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.820
Super Tuesdays, results that that hurt Bernie.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.310
And the second Super Tuesday and the third
Super Tuesday and the virus ultimately keeping

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:40.670
people at home.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:48.521
And AOC has also publicly shifted from being
very antagonistic towards Nancy Pelosi, the

00:01:48.521 --> 00:01:53.660
Democratic speaker of the House, to being
more publicly laudatory and positive towards

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.340
Nancy Pelosi.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.880
And a lot of people have jumped on her for
this.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:03.070
AOC has also jumped into criticizing Bernie
supporters for online harassment.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:08.240
That's been mostly the purview of centrist
Democrats and Biden supporters and sort of

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.240
DNC folks.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:13.099
But AOC has said, yeah, you know, a lot of
that online harassment is not good.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:17.569
She said some of Bernie's allies are too conflict
based.

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:21.220
That also rubbed a lot of Bernie supporters
the wrong way.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:27.769
AOC also launched a PAC earlier this year,
which is not looking to primary centrist Democrats.

00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:31.260
It's focused on flipping red states to blue.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:36.520
The goal of AOSIS PAC is not to find centrist
Democrats and replace them.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:41.280
It's to find red seats and turn them blue,
replacing Republicans with Democrats.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:50.040
Now, I have to tell you, this makes me see
AOC as much more clever and shrewd politically

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.560
as a political operative than I imagined you
guys.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:58.150
Many of you criticize me occasionally for
saying, hey, you know, AOC has a lot of the

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:04.439
right ideas, but not the right political practicality,
not the right political approach.

00:03:04.439 --> 00:03:05.860
I see that as changing here.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.879
Now, there's lots of people that are furious
about this.

00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:10.830
Tea Whitey host Janke Yuga has gone after
AOC for this.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.060
A bunch of others have.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.739
But let's think this through.

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:17.060
First of all, almost everyone changes when
they got elected.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:23.170
And this is why I always say don't DFI or
glorify individual politicians.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.790
They are all elected by the system we currently
have.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:30.669
And essentially every single one of them,
to some degree it varies.

00:03:30.669 --> 00:03:36.370
But to some degree, when they become elected
officials under that system, they will start

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:42.700
to really reinforce or defend to some degree
some elements of the system that got them

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.529
elected once they get into power.

00:03:44.529 --> 00:03:46.209
That applies to just about everybody.

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:50.069
It doesn't mean that they flip and abandon
their values.

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:51.359
That's not what I'm saying.

00:03:51.359 --> 00:03:54.219
But that's not the important analysis for
me.

00:03:54.219 --> 00:04:01.209
The important analysis for me is that we just
got done talking about Bernie lost, not because

00:04:01.209 --> 00:04:07.040
his ideas are bad, but because a lot of the
people around him are toxic because of his

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.919
relationship with those in positions of power,
because the country just isn't as overtly

00:04:11.919 --> 00:04:13.579
left as Bernie Sanders.

00:04:13.579 --> 00:04:18.290
For the last six weeks, we've been saying
many of us, the future of the progressive

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.290
movement.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:21.489
Is in somebody with Bernie's sensibilities.

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:22.949
Bernie's values.

00:04:22.949 --> 00:04:25.419
Many of Bernie's policy goals.

00:04:25.419 --> 00:04:27.400
But who has a better team around them?

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.410
Fewer toxic people.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.410
Better branding.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.000
None of this democratic socialist stuff.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.280
The revolution language is not particularly
useful to Bernie.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.330
AOC isn't changing her political positions
here.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.580
Her view on Medicare for all hasn't changed.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.650
Her view on the Green New Deal hasn't changed.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.240
She's changing her approach.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.759
Maybe at least that's what it seems like.

00:04:46.759 --> 00:04:48.669
This is what we've been talking about, guys.

00:04:48.669 --> 00:04:53.610
We don't need someone who differs from Bernie
on core values.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:55.530
Bernie has the right core values.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.880
AOC shares Bernie's core values.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.289
Nothing has changed as far as that goes.

00:05:00.289 --> 00:05:03.750
AOC is doing exactly what Bernie didn't do.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:10.889
AOC is doing something to get around what
ultimately led to Bernie getting crushed on

00:05:10.889 --> 00:05:14.930
Super Tuesday and then more on Super Tuesday
2 and more on Super Tuesday 3.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:19.080
People keep saying, hey, we need Bernie's
ideas with better framing, packaging and public

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.080
relations.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.960
That's what AOC is leaning towards here.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:28.120
AOC is looking to become a force for change
by building these relationships where in the

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:34.520
next six years, eight years, she could have
a long laundry list of legislative accomplishments.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.490
She's working within the system to invoke
change.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:39.550
Now, that's an area of disagreement.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:45.129
Bernie has more of an approach of destroying
the system revolution and then rebuilding

00:05:45.129 --> 00:05:47.159
it from the ground up.

00:05:47.159 --> 00:05:51.330
Working within the system has gotten us many
important things.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:56.800
Gay Marriage, Violence Against Women Act,
food stamps, Social Security, Consumer Financial

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:01.470
Protection Bureau, preexisting conditions,
coverage and being on your parents insurance

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:02.509
until age 26.

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:03.940
Labor laws, birth control.

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:05.470
Now, has it been enough?

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:06.470
No.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.520
No way in hell has it also led to bad things.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.520
Of course.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.569
I mean, you know, look at the Iraq war.

00:06:11.569 --> 00:06:19.130
The Iraq war is the epitome of working within
the system with centrist Democrats in great

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.850
part that got us the Iraq war.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:28.310
But when I see AOC step away from some of
the absolutism of Bernie.

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:36.169
My feeling is this will help her get things
done rather than being able to say, we tried

00:06:36.169 --> 00:06:37.169
this, but we failed.

00:06:37.169 --> 00:06:39.020
We didn't actually get to do it.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:44.580
I believe this better positions AOC to actually
get things done.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:50.219
To me, this suggests AOSIS political instincts
are better than I thought.

00:06:50.219 --> 00:06:54.419
I underestimated her political instincts until
I saw this.

00:06:54.419 --> 00:06:56.110
I'm ready to get crushed, my friends.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:58.449
I'm ready for people to disagree.

00:06:58.449 --> 00:07:01.360
Tell me all the ways in which I am wrong.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:40.819
But this this actually improves my opinion

00:07:40.819 --> 00:07:58.409
of

00:07:58.409 --> 00:08:05.580
AOC dramatically.

